    "note": "The reference and the two duty-cycle channels, which together are the DAC's accuracy. HR5 carries the 13 V reference -- two cascaded 6.5 V temperature-compensated transistor/zener ref amps, biased by a thin-film network so their temperature coefficients cancel -- on a substrate heated to 62 °C by Q1 and Q2 on the main board, with RT2 inside the hybrid stealing base current at about 67 °C to stop a thermal runaway. The coarse channel switches that 13 V through series FETs Q4/Q5 and shunt FET Q6; the fine channel switches a 3 V rail, buffered by U1B and U11, through Q30 and Q32 and then divides it by about 3800 inside HR5. Two correction circuits exist purely because those FETs have 3 to 5 Ω of on-resistance: U38 with Z2 supplies the series switch's filter current, U2B with Q22 and three 80 kΩ resistors in HR6 supplies the shunt switch's.",
